CAT = "abatWorking"; SEG = "WRK"
Q = [
("A client gets upset each time the session moves from table work to play. Which support usually helps?",
 "A countdown before each transition", ["Surprise transitions to avoid fuss", "Longer table time with no breaks", "Skipping play to avoid changes"],
 "Many autistic clients find unexpected change hard, and a warning or countdown makes the change predictable. Dropping play removes a reinforcer and does not teach the transition."),
("A client takes words literally. Which instruction is clearest for him?",
 "\"Put the blocks in the box\"", ["\"Let's hop to it with the blocks\"", "\"Those blocks won't clean themselves\"", "\"Can you maybe think about the blocks?\""],
 "Plain, literal instructions say exactly what to do. Idioms, hints and questions phrased as suggestions can be read literally and miss the point."),
("Before placing any demands on a new client, the ABAT plays with the client's favorite toys and hands out treats freely. This is called:",
 "Pairing", ["Demand fading", "Extinction", "Response cost"],
 "Pairing builds the ABAT's value as a source of good things, so later instructions come from someone the client already enjoys being with."),
("A client asks for juice by pressing a button on his speech device. What should the ABAT do?",
 "Honor it like a spoken request", ["Make him say the word first", "Keep the device out of sessions", "Ask him to use the device later"],
 "A request made with an AAC device is real communication. Requiring speech first punishes the client's way of communicating."),
("The plan allows noise-reducing headphones. A client covers his ears in a loud gym. What fits the plan?",
 "Offer the listed headphones", ["Make him stay without them", "Scold him for covering his ears", "Take him off the gym schedule"],
 "Following the plan's sensory support meets his need. Removing him from the gym schedule would change the plan, which is the supervisor's decision."),
("A client loves trains. How can this interest help teaching?",
 "Build trains into teaching tasks", ["Ban trains so he can focus", "Allow trains only after sessions", "Talk about trains to fill time"],
 "Using a strong interest in materials and examples raises motivation. Banning it wastes a powerful reinforcer."),
("A \"first work, then tablet\" board helps a client mainly because it:",
 "Shows what comes next", ["Removes all demands", "Punishes refusals", "Replaces reinforcement"],
 "A first-then board makes the sequence visible and links the task to the reward that follows it."),
("Staff are discussing a minimally verbal teen while he sits in the room. What is best practice?",
 "Speak as if he understands", ["Speak freely since he cannot follow", "Spell out the private words", "Lower your voice slightly"],
 "Limited speech does not mean limited understanding. Talking about him as if he were absent harms dignity and privacy."),
("After giving an instruction, why does the ABAT wait a few seconds before prompting?",
 "Some clients need time to process", ["Waiting always prevents errors", "It lowers the client's motivation", "It replaces the need for praise"],
 "Many clients need extra processing time. Prompting too soon can build prompt dependence, though waiting does not guarantee a correct answer."),
("A client rocks quietly while working, and the plan does not target rocking. What should the ABAT do?",
 "Let it continue as planned", ["Block each rock", "Use response cost for rocking", "Start a plan to reduce it"],
 "Not every repetitive movement is a target. Harmless rocking that does not interfere is left alone unless the supervisor adds it to the plan."),
("A client is crying and overwhelmed after a fire alarm. What comes first?",
 "Help him feel safe and calm", ["Present the next work task", "Withhold all reinforcers", "Keep teaching and record data"],
 "A distressed client is not ready to learn. Calming and safety come before demands resume."),
("Why should every staff member follow the same steps when teaching one skill to a client?",
 "Consistency speeds learning", ["Different styles prevent boredom", "It removes the need for data", "It is only a billing rule"],
 "Consistency makes the right response easier to learn. Generalization across people and places is planned on purpose, not left to random differences in teaching."),
]
